data: {"level":2,"reviewed":{"level":2,"label":"formula / approach","text":"Partition by account. Order by the timestamp and then the posting identifier, so that each posting\nhas a unique position. The balance after a posting is the sum over the positions up to it: a frame from the first row\nto the current row. Once the order is unique, the default frame gives the same totals, so the\nchoice of frame is yours, and an explicit `ROWS` frame is the clearest way to state it."},"hints_note":null}

